# The WebAssembly export surface.
#
# Kept separate from the core modules for the same reason pymodule_exports.elisa
# is: this file names a target-specific ABI. `export fn` gives each function
# external linkage so it survives -O2 (the backend prefers private linkage when
# optimising, which otherwise strips everything the shell wants to call).
#
# Built by scripts/build_wasm.sh; run by shells/web/elisa-wasm-runtime.js.
# Runtime include roots are resolved from ELISA_STAGE1_ROOT by the WASM build
# scripts. This keeps the Stage0 oracle and Stage1 candidate on the exact same
# selected compiler runtime rather than silently importing a stale sibling
# checkout.

# Use the runtime fragments needed by this single-threaded browser target.
# The aggregate runtime also includes native thread/pool APIs; the port does
# not call those APIs, and the newest Stage1 correctly refuses to emit their
# unsupported WebAssembly bodies instead of silently producing a partial
# object. Keep the supported runtime surface explicit until a WASI concurrency
# backend is implemented and exercised by a real port use site.
